1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,200
Glimpse: what's new. Here are the newer features, with the real extension.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:11,200
Theme: choose Dark, Light or System in Settings.
The answer cards, side panel and options all follow it.

3
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:20,200
The side menu now has 13 tools: Chat, Hand, Code, REC Note,
Translate, Summarize, ChatPDF, Write, Painter, OCR,
Grammar, Email Reply and Text to Speech.

4
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:29,200
New Groq provider: paste your key (it stays hidden)...
...and the model list loads straight from your own key.

5
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:36,200
Copy any text (Ctrl+C) and the answer card opens
to explain it, right where you are reading.

6
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:46,200
Answer from screenshot: a floating card you can drag around.
Pin it, rate the answer with thumbs up or down,
and use the camera button to snap a region.

7
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:53,200
Web Control, scraping: ask in plain words and Glimpse
extracts tables, links and prices, ready as CSV or JSON.

8
00:00:53,800 --> 00:01:01,200
Web Control, auto form fill: Glimpse fills the form from your profile.
You preview it and press submit yourself.

9
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:11,200
Take over browser: it asks your permission first.
While it works you get a glowing border, a status pill
with a Stop button, and a live step log.

10
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:19,200
Press Stop at any time. When it finishes, you get the result,
here 18 laptops with names and prices.

11
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:23,700
Try it: github.com/panther1345/Glimpse
